 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Threshold is 0.9 V minimum and 2.0 V maximum, taken at 250 μA with gate and drain tied. On-resistance is specified at two gate voltages: 90 mΩ typical, 105 mΩ maximum at 10 V and 3 A; 92 mΩ typical, 125 mΩ maximum at 4.5 V and 2 A. Normalized to 25 °C it rises to about 1.83 at 150 °C (10 V, 3 A). The gate is rated ±20 V; leakage is at most ±100 nA at ±20 V and ±50 nA at ±10 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Total gate charge is 6 nC typical at 4.5 V on the gate and 30 V on the drain, of which 1 nC is gate-source and 1.3 nC gate-drain. With a 10 V drive through 6 Ω, 30 V and 3 A, delays are 6 ns on and 15 ns off, rise 15 ns and fall 10 ns."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The drain-source body diode conducts up to 3.0 A continuously and drops 0.9 V typical, 1.2 V maximum at 3.0 A. Reverse recovery at 3.0 A and 100 A/μs takes 32.6 ns with 6.99 nC of charge, both typical."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Junction-to-ambient thermal resistance is 104 °C/W. Dissipation is 1.2 W with the ambient at 25 °C and 0.8 W at 100 °C; continuous drain current is 3.0 A and 2.4 A at those ambients, falling to zero at 150 °C. Junction and storage temperature span -55 °C to +150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Trench low-voltage process with dense cells for low on-resistance. The SOT-23 mold compound has a UL 94V-0 flammability rating and is RoHS-compliant and halogen-free. Leads are solder plated; their solderability meets MIL-STD-750 method 2026."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Applications: battery protection, load switching and power management. Switching is fast."
  }
 ],
